WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.660
- All right, everybody.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.870
It is time for Drew's News.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.300
When life flattens your
tires, we'll pump 'em back up

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.460
with that good news air. (mimics air pump)

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.450
(Ross laughs)
Well, with me at the desk

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:13.580
is my dearest friend,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.010
who I know could always change any tire,

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.285
it's Ross Matthews.

00:00:17.285 --> 00:00:19.176
(audience applauds)
- No, call a different friend.

00:00:19.176 --> 00:00:20.420
(Ross mimics laser gun)

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.757
- I know.
- I couldn't do that.

00:00:22.757 --> 00:00:25.340
- Do you keep a jack in your car?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.710
- I don't even know if
I keep a jack in my,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:28.860
sorry, what's a jack?

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:29.710
I don't know.
(audience laughs)

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.760
My dad was a mechanic
and you would've thought

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.730
that he would've taught
me how to change a tire

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.213
and maybe he tried, but
I was not interested.

00:00:36.213 --> 00:00:38.103
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:40.310
(audience applauds)
- Okay, Ross, your story.

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:41.880
- Well, here's a fun story.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.830
A really fun one.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:45.700
There's a brand new job
opening up at Buckingham Palace

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.533
and Drew Barrymore,

00:00:46.533 --> 00:00:49.110
I feel like you might need
to apply for this one.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.880
Apartment Therapy reports The
Queen is hiring a decorator.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.650
She wants to redecorate
the entire Royal household

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:58.230
room by room.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.070
So she's, she's looking for someone

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.730
with a passion for
historic buildings, check.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.120
Good communication skills, check, check.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.370
And a natural team player,
check, check, check.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:10.250
The job pays $40,000 a year.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.182
It has full benefits and a pension

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:15.688
and you get 33 days off a year.

00:01:15.688 --> 00:01:17.140
(audience gasp and applaud)

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.480
All right.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.570
So Madam, is this a job you'd want?

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.760
And what would you do with it?

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.690
- I love designing so much
(audience applauds)

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.050
- [Ross] You've got a great aesthetic.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.040
- I wanna get her one of those
neon signs above her bed.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.968
That just says, "Yas Queen"

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.385
(they laugh)

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.540
I gotta figure it out.

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.270
- I love that.
- Yeah. Right.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:40.800
- But who would not want
to work as a designer?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.770
You're out there making
people's spaces brighter

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:47.520
and happier places for them to be.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.680
Queen or no Queen, I'm in.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:50.690
- Yeah, I think so too.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.370
And I think it's time for
the whole Royal family.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.330
They need a little refresh
on everything, right?

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.620
So let's start with a little decor.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.352
(audience applauds)
- Well, this is

00:01:58.352 --> 00:02:00.797
a story I found and I thought,

00:02:00.797 --> 00:02:02.650
"Oh, I have to bring this to the desk."

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.000
Okay, so attention, New Yorkers.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.840
We are officially the first
city where this is happening.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.580
Uber is joining forces with Yellow Cabs.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.180
The New York Times reports
that starting this spring

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:19.840
Uber will allow you to order
a yellow taxi on their app.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.440
They're teaming up with the
two apps that already exist

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.200
for Yellow Cab, Curb and CMT.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.580
And if you order a Yellow Cab on Uber,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:31.760
you'll pay Uber rates,
including surge prices.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.593
- Wah-wah.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:34.720
- What do you think?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.710
- Well, I think we have to,

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.070
they have to make this kind of change,

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.400
'cause it's a brand new world.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.233
I just have to say

00:02:39.233 --> 00:02:42.420
as somebody with a proud 4.89 Uber rating.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.390
I hope that this doesn't affect it,

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.630
because I'm really proud of that.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.470
I do have to say, I am.
(audience applauds)

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.063
4.89 is good.

00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:54.990
- I don't know what my Uber rating is.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.160
I know that I'm a happy passenger.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.620
- Yeah.
- But I feel like

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.500
I'm also a late to get
downstairs passenger.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.660
- Oh, that's gonna affect your score.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.180
4.89. That means I'm
polite, I'm courteous.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.380
I talk, but I don't over talk. (laughs)

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.800
- Do you choose the talk to
me or don't talk to me button?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.379
- I let them figure it out.

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:17.457
You know what I mean?

00:03:17.457 --> 00:03:20.180
- So you say "Yes, I allow conversation."

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.230
- Express yourself through Uber.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.720
- Okay, How many hands,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.010
show raise of hands say no to conversation

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:27.843
on your Uber app?

00:03:27.843 --> 00:03:29.460
Right there. Proud, I love it.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.620
I'm sorry.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.480
Aren't you glad you raised your hand now?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:34.360
Okay, why do you do it?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.310
- [Lady] I talk about this
all the time to my coworkers,

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.690
because I work overnight shifts

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.570
and I just feel like
that's a no conversation.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.620
Like, it's acceptable.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.070
It should be acceptable.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.520
- Yeah.
- Yes, to me.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.435
- And you like that option?
(audience applauds)

00:03:50.435 --> 00:03:51.602
- I love that.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.200
I like your approach.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.783
(bright music)

